userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: Whether a solid conducts electricity depends on the size of the band gap between its filled valence band and empty conduction band — the smaller the gap, the easier it is to promote electrons and the better it conducts.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Electrical conduction in a solid is governed by a single number — the band gap energy — because an electron can only carry current after being promoted across that gap from the filled valence band into the conduction band.
DEMO STEPS: 3 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
